tools/cardkit is ported from cashucard's tools/cardkit
(https://github.com/cashucard/cashucard, package 0.2.0, main at 0229dc8).
The files below are copied as they are at that commit:

    gp/apdu.ts           copied verbatim
    gp/bytes.ts          copied verbatim
    gp/des.ts            copied verbatim
    gp/scp03.ts          copied verbatim
    gp/test/node-aes.ts  copied verbatim from testing/node-aes.ts
    gp/test/node-des.ts  copied verbatim from testing/node-des.ts
    gp/test/transcript.ts
                         copied verbatim
    gp/test/fixtures/scp03-07-list-default-keyver1.txt,
    gp/test/fixtures/scp03-08-list-default-auto.txt,
    gp/test/fixtures/scp03-09-install-probe-default-key.txt,
    gp/test/fixtures/scp03-10-delete-probe-default-key.txt
                         copied verbatim: the owner's captures of the J3R452
                         under the public default keys

These differ only in the statements named:

    gp/scp02.ts          one line: a comment says this card's DELETE whitelist
                         holds three AIDs rather than Cashu's six
    gp/test/des.test.ts  one line: the import path of node-des, and the
                         import's multi-line layout, which is kept
                         verbatim against this repo's prettier settings so
                         the file stays diffable against upstream (it is
                         listed in .prettierignore for that reason)
    gp/test/scp03.test.ts
                         the import path of node-aes, and the comment that
                         names it
    gp/test/rotate.test.ts
                         the import path of the fake card, and the comment
                         that says where ROTATION_AT_01's hashes come from

These are adapted:

    gp/test/scp02.test.ts
                         this card's AIDs and byte-for-byte literals, and the
                         whitelist test names three AIDs
    gp/provision.ts      rotateKeys, its options and RotateResult.firstContact,
                         and the first-contact checks of the key information,
                         as upstream has them without the sdAid run option;
                         the install is this project's (below)
    gp/test/fake-card.ts upstream's SCP03 card side (scp, keySet,
                         keepsShippedSet, sellerApplets and SELLER_APPLETS,
                         GET DATA E0) merged into this project's fake of the
                         Fedimint applet, without the isd and cplc options
    gp/test/transcripts.test.ts
                         the SCP03 section and the two readings of the key
                         information template, as upstream has them; not the
                         H0 section, whose J3R180 captures are not here; and
                         one case of this project's own
    gp/test/fixtures/README.md
                         the J3R452 section and its four rows

These are ported with changes of their own:

    gp/identity.ts       cashucard's parseCplc and readChipIdentity, without
                         the expected-id check (ops keys each card's manager
                         keys on the id instead)
    gp/test/identity.test.ts
                         the same J3R180 CPLC capture, and the refusals

Everything else in tools/cardkit is written for this project: the install's
plan and key-set candidates in gp/provision.ts, gp/reset.ts (this card's
factory reset, not cashucard's owned-card reset), gp/aids.ts,
gp/load-file.ts and the rest of the tests. The upstream code it does not need
(the registry, inspect, reset-preflight, settled-cleanup, configuration and
holderCommands modules, the cleanup entry point, the install's handling of
the seller's NDEF tag, and the NFC tag and hello applets) was not ported.

